+# Project rules
+
+The rules this project follows. Every change follows them.
+
+## Rules
+
+### No new runtime dependency
+
+Do not add a package to `dependencies` in `package.json`: the project's runtime dependencies are the
+ones it already has. Development tools may go in `devDependencies`.
+
+### TSDoc on every exported function
+
+Every exported function has a TSDoc comment, `/** … */`, right before it: what it does, and what its
+parameters are.
+
+### No wall clock or randomness in the domain
+
+Code under `src/domain/` does not read the clock or make random values: no `Date.now()`, no
+`new Date()` without arguments, no `Math.random()`, no random identifiers.
+
+### Errors are returned as a Result in the domain
+
+Code under `src/domain/` never throws: an operation that can fail returns a `Result`, with an error
+that says what went wrong.
+
+### About the project
+
+- `tidy-tasks`: the in-memory task list behind the Tidy Tasks to-do app (tasks have a title, a priority
+  `low|normal|high`, tags and a status `open|done`). The app's screens use only the public API exported
+  from `src/index.ts`; a new capability is reachable only if it is exported there.
+- TypeScript (ES2022, ESM, `strict`, `NodeNext`), run directly by Node with type stripping: imports of
+  local files use the `.ts` extension, and only erasable syntax is allowed (no `enum`, no namespaces, no
+  constructor parameter properties). No build step; `package.json` has no runtime dependencies.
+- Layout: `src/domain/task.ts` (task type and pure task functions), `src/domain/list.ts` (the in-memory
+  list, `createTaskList`), `src/domain/result.ts` (`Result`, `ok`, `err`, `valueOr`, `TodoErrorCode`),
+  `src/domain/summary.ts` (`summarize`), `src/index.ts` (public API), `test/*.test.ts` (tests).
+- Tests: `npm test` (`node --test`, `node:test` with `node:assert/strict`, in `test/*.test.ts`, importing
+  from `../src/index.ts`). Run it before calling work done; add or update tests for every behaviour
+  change, including each failure path of a new operation.
+
+### Conventions
+
+- Data is immutable: types use `readonly` fields and `readonly` arrays; task functions return a new
+  object rather than changing the one given.
+- Task titles are trimmed, and are the key of the list (each title once). Tags keep the order given, each once.
+- Failures use the existing `TodoErrorCode`s (`not-found`, `duplicate`, `invalid-state`); add a code to
+  `result.ts` only when none fits. Error messages are written for the person using the app.
+- Pure task logic goes in `task.ts` and returns `Result` where it can fail; `list.ts` stores and
+  composes it. Types the app needs are re-exported from `src/index.ts`.
+- Exported interfaces, types and constants get a one-line `/** … */` comment, as the existing ones have.
+  Parameter docs use `@param name - what it is`.
+- Style: single quotes, semicolons, 2-space indent, trailing commas in multi-line literals, `ok(...)`
+  and `err(code, message)` to build results, results checked with `if (!result.ok) return result;`.
+- Display order of tasks: open before done, then most urgent first, then by title (`compareTasks`).
+
+## Rules per artifact
+
+### proposal
+
+- State which of the project's rules above the change touches, and how it stays within them.
+- Say whether the public API in `src/index.ts` changes.
+
+### specs
+
+- Write requirements about behaviour a person using the app can observe, including the failure cases and their error codes.
+
+### design
+
+- Keep the domain pure and free of clock and randomness; if a time or an identifier is needed, it is passed in by the caller.
+- Do not plan a new runtime dependency.
+
+### tasks
+
+- Include a task to add or update tests in `test/` for each behaviour, and a final task to run `npm test`.
+- Include a task for TSDoc on each new exported function, and for exporting new public types or functions from `src/index.ts` when the app needs them.
